  "goodToKnow": "Der Demokrat (die Demokratin) is a democrat, someone who supports democracy: ein überzeugter Demokrat. In US politics, die Demokraten are the Democratic Party. It's a weak noun: den Demokraten. Germany calls itself a wehrhafte Demokratie (a democracy that can defend itself), meaning parties that fight the constitution can be banned. From Greek demos (people) and kratos (power)."
